Subject: [PATCH 139/140] =?UTF-8?q?feat(people):=20the=20path=20map=20sear?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ches=20members=20only,=20so=20a=20longer=20all-member=20path=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?is=20found=20(1849=20stage=20one,=20=C2=A7127)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

0113 read the graph's shortest paths and kept those whose every middle
person is a member; when each shortest path ran through somebody not on
Netai, a longer all-member path was never looked for. The middles are now
read from the members' own phonebooks — the owner's members, the members
who have the target saved, and up to one member between them — so every
path found can be carried, up to three in the middle. Each person is
named by the phone the person before them saved. Blocks, warm steps and
the ranking are as in 0113.

The three-step read was timed read-only on production with the largest
member phonebook: 1.7 s, inside its 8 s timeout. NETAI_ACTIVE_SUBSCRIPTION_STATUSES
is exported so the SQL membership test uses the same list.

